{% block focus %}
Find published prices for comparable offers (competitors, substitutes, platforms), and any evidence of what this customer actually pays. Record every price as a numeric claim with unit EUR or EUR/<unit>, and state whether it includes VAT.

Search strategy:
1. Fetch the price lists of the competitors and substitutes you can find, local first, then North Karelia and Finland, then online.
2. Platforms and marketplaces (booking sites, tori.fi, Etsy, REKO groups) for the prices customers actually see; note the platform fee separately.
3. The price trend of the category from Statistics Finland's consumer price index (`pxweb search "kuluttajahintaindeksi"`), when a trend matters for the plan.

Finnish search terms: `hinnasto`, `hinta`, `alkaen`, `€/h`, `sis. alv`, `alv 0 %`, `veroton hinta`, `tarjous`, `kampanja`.

Finnish data tools for this dimension: `pxweb` (consumer price index for the category's trend); prices themselves come from the sellers' own pages.
